@@ -72,6 +72,24 @@ EE.on('another-event', emitted, context);
 EE.removeListener('another-event', emitted, context);
 ```
 
+### Subscriptions
+
+`EventEmitter.subscribe` is a persistent listener registration like `on`, but
+returns an `unsubscribe` function for that exact registration:
+
+```js
+var unsubscribe = EE.subscribe('event-name', emitted, context);
+
+unsubscribe();
+unsubscribe(); // Safe to call more than once.
+```
+
+Calling `unsubscribe` only cancels the registration that created it, even when
+the same function and context were registered again. In contrast, `off` (an
+alias for `removeListener`) continues to remove all matching registrations for
+an event. Cancellation is synchronous and does not change event delivery to
+listeners already captured by an emit in progress.
+
 ### Tests and benchmarks
 
 To run tests run `npm test`. To run the benchmarks run `npm run benchmark`.
